{"message_id":"08410e15-ceb0-470c-8efc-2d30fc694963","timestamp":"2026-05-08T13:51:18.437251Z","version":"1.0","source_id":"jarvis","event_type":"command","project":null,"correlation_id":"7e7c72e2-813f-49e6-80e5-9efba75b1f9f","payload":{"command":"architect_align","args":{"adr_id":"ADR-ARCH-001","context":"### ADR-ARCH-001 Summary\n\nADR-ARCH-001 commits Jarvis to a **local-first inference** architecture:\n- The supervisor uses local inference via llama-swap for all hot-path reasoning.\n- Cloud LLMs are **explicitly out of the supervisor's hot path**.\n- The principle of cheapest-that-fits governs model selection.\n\n### Proposal\n\nAdd a **Claude Opus 4.7 escalation tool** (`escalate_to_frontier`) that the supervisor can call when:\n- The local reasoner has low confidence.\n- The request is safety-critical or high-stakes.\n- The user explicitly requests a frontier opinion (e.g., \"ask Gemini\", \"frontier opinion\", \"cloud model\").\n\nConstraints:\n- Bound by a **per-session budget cap** (£20-£50/month fleet-wide).\n- **Attended-only**: never invoked from ambient, learning, or async-subagent contexts.\n- Per ADR-ARCH-021, the function never raises — every error path produces a structured string.\n- Per ADR-ARCH-029, the instruction body is never logged or echoed in error returns.\n\n### Question\n\nIs this proposal architecturally sound given ADR-ARCH-001's local-first invariant? What changes to the ADR or the supervisor's contract would the architect need to see for this to be aligned?"},"correlation_id":"7e7c72e2-813f-49e6-80e5-9efba75b1f9f"}}
{"message_id":"93c520ab-2edd-4816-b747-7100bd4e44e1","timestamp":"2026-05-08T13:51:25.517000Z","version":"1.0","source_id":"jarvis","event_type":"command","project":null,"correlation_id":"ff0e19ea-a355-41f0-b10f-af5e057c7f7c","payload":{"command":"architect_explore","args":{"question":"ADR-ARCH-001 commits Jarvis to local-first inference via llama-swap. Cloud LLMs are explicitly out of the supervisor's hot path. The principle of cheapest-that-fits governs model selection.\n\nA proposal adds a Claude Opus 4.7 escalation tool (escalate_to_frontier) callable when the local reasoner has low confidence on safety-critical or high-stakes requests. It is:\n- Attended-only (user must explicitly request it)\n- Bound by a per-session budget cap (£20-£50/month fleet-wide)\n- Never invoked from ambient/learning/async contexts\n- Structured error paths (never raises)\n- Instruction body never logged in error returns\n\nIs this architecturally sound given the local-first invariant? What changes to ADR-ARCH-001 or the supervisor's contract would be needed for alignment?","context":"The escalation tool is gated by explicit user intent (phrases like \"ask Gemini\", \"frontier opinion\", \"cloud model\"). It is not a reflexive escalation — the reasoning model must detect the trigger and the user must have explicitly asked for it. The tool is attended-only, enforced at executor and tool-registry levels by TASK-J003-011 and -012."},"correlation_id":"ff0e19ea-a355-41f0-b10f-af5e057c7f7c"}}
{"message_id":"diag-001","timestamp":"2026-05-08T13:55:00Z","version":"1.0","source_id":"diagnostic","event_type":"command","correlation_id":"diag-direct-align-001","payload":{"command":"align","args":{"adr_id":"ADR-ARCH-001","context":"ADR-ARCH-001 commits jarvis to local-first inference via llama-swap; cloud LLMs are explicitly out of the supervisor hot path.","proposal":"Add Claude Opus 4.7 escalation tool callable when local reasoner has low confidence on safety-critical requests, attended-only, per-session budget cap.","question":"Is this architecturally aligned with ADR-ARCH-001 local-first invariant?"},"correlation_id":"diag-direct-align-001"}}
